{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_data/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:07:28.797612Z","id":"e0e740c3cdfdfce77d40916d6c2257c4967a5e23fa09b847a1ba140e64741e63","body":{"detail":"MovingAppData keeps each store's fold mark in memory only (crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs catch_up), so after a restart each artifact's first call makes an extra AppDataOp::FoldMark call when any fold was ever logged. A fold below every store's mark could be pruned once every artifact has moved and caught up.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":40},"content_hash":"3acec9267f6fe13218326f7ab0e69e619d74ef3cdd1d04fc8b16d481ee8813d8"},"summary":"app_data_folds is never pruned: one row per viewer claim, and every artifact store's first call in a process asks its fold mark while the log is non-empty","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_data/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.530120Z","id":"3981f831385c40d6ec575806a6f0651da877d1124a74b10aef1ba543d990ee0f","body":{"detail":"Each job step's and ClaxBot call's document write leaves a row (op_id, digest, reply, at) in the artifact's own store. A retry needs only the rows of steps and calls not yet journaled in the instance; the rest are dead weight that grows with every write made under an ID.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"8d470560e813d94a2bae1b198d4b7b1dcca974b16f8939d8e7199918d087d5ec"},"suggested_fix":"Prune rows older than the longest a job or bot run may be resumed (the 'at' column), or have the instance send the IDs it has journaled.","summary":"applied_ops keeps every operation ID an artifact store ever answered, with its reply, and nothing prunes it","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_data/instance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:24.349168Z","id":"9f1e54fd208db235e9bfbc498b275546624f268e247ca12f83860daae3168d29","body":{"detail":"MovingAppData keeps each store's fold mark in memory only (crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs catch_up), so after a restart each artifact's first call makes an extra AppDataOp::FoldMark call when any fold was ever logged. A fold below every store's mark could be pruned once every artifact has moved and caught up.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"3acec9267f6fe13218326f7ab0e69e619d74ef3cdd1d04fc8b16d481ee8813d8"},"summary":"app_data_folds is never pruned: one row per viewer claim, and every artifact store's first call in a process asks its fold mark while the log is non-empty","supersedes":"e0e740c3cdfdfce77d40916d6c2257c4967a5e23fa09b847a1ba140e64741e63","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
